<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    ADAPTED COPY of the file the Sulu skeleton generates at
    sulu/config/webspaces/website.xml (see FIXES.md No. 44).

    It lives here in sulu-overlay/ so that "make sulu-theme" copies it
    into ./sulu before "sulu:build dev" initialises PHPCR - the order in
    the Makefile's sulu-install target matters, because the content tree
    is set up for whatever localizations exist at that moment.

    WHAT WAS CHANGED versus the skeleton original - two functional
    changes:
      1. <localization language="de" default="true"/>  (was: "en")
      2. <url language="de">{host}</url> in all four environments
         (was: language="en")
    Plus cosmetics with no effect on behaviour: the skeleton's
    doc-link comments and its commented-out <excluded-templates>
    example block were dropped, and the <title> order under
    <navigation> now puts German first.

    WHY: this is a DACH storefront. The skeleton ships English as the
    only content localization, so every page was stored in an "en"
    language slot even though all the text in it is German, and Sulu's
    admin showed "en" in the language switcher. Sulu doesn't enforce a
    match between the locale code and the actual text language, so this
    was cosmetically wrong rather than broken - but wrong is wrong for a
    project meant to be handed to a team.

    NO URL PREFIX results from this: a <url> tag mapped to exactly one
    localization serves it at the bare host (per Sulu's own webspace
    documentation). Only the {localization} placeholder form generates
    per-language URL prefixes. So the Caddy routes are unaffected.

    "de" rather than "de_DE": adding a country attribute
    (<localization language="de" country="de"/>) would produce the
    locale code "de-de". For a single-language webspace the plain form
    is the simpler correct one. Note this is independent of Sylius'
    channel locales (de_DE / de_AT / de_CH) - those live in the Sylius
    app and are unrelated to Sulu's content localization.

    MAINTENANCE NOTE: because this shadows a skeleton-generated file, a
    future Sulu update that changes the original will NOT show up here.
    Compare the two after any Sulu upgrade - same fragility as the
    bundle-template overrides in FIXES.md No. 36.
-->
<webspace xmlns="http://schemas.sulu.io/webspace/webspace"
          xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
          xsi:schemaLocation="http://schemas.sulu.io/webspace/webspace http://schemas.sulu.io/webspace/webspace-1.1.xsd">

    <name>Website</name>
    <key>website</key>

    <localizations>
        <localization language="de" default="true"/>
    </localizations>

    <default-templates>
        <default-template type="page">default</default-template>
        <default-template type="home">homepage</default-template>
    </default-templates>

    <templates>
        <template type="search">search/search</template>
        <template type="error">error/error</template>
    </templates>

    <navigation>
        <contexts>
            <context key="main">
                <meta>
                    <title lang="de">Hauptnavigation</title>
                    <title lang="en">Main Navigation</title>
                </meta>
            </context>
        </contexts>
    </navigation>

    <portals>
        <portal>
            <name>Website</name>
            <key>website</key>

            <environments>
                <environment type="prod">
                    <urls>
                        <url language="de">{host}</url>
                    </urls>
                </environment>
                <environment type="stage">
                    <urls>
                        <url language="de">{host}</url>
                    </urls>
                </environment>
                <environment type="test">
                    <urls>
                        <url language="de">{host}</url>
                    </urls>
                </environment>
                <environment type="dev">
                    <urls>
                        <url language="de">{host}</url>
                    </urls>
                </environment>
            </environments>
        </portal>
    </portals>
</webspace>
